{"parentUuid":"91ccf4a3-563b-4e9e-aa79-3f5875e7dd0e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"624a8cec-33fa-4c0a-a445-c72ce718e6ab","agentId":"a07e06bc199bf998d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# Review: Supertraining Ch4.3-4.4 (23 entries), falsification pass\n\nReviewer: Claude Opus (independent of the writer). Date: 2026-10-03.\nSource: *Supertraining* 6th Expanded, PDF idx 252-265 (printed 241-254). Page key: PDF idx = printed + 11.\nMethod: text layer extracted with pymupdf for every covered page; page images rendered at 150 dpi and opened for PDF 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 260, 261, 262, 263, 264 (every figure, table and equation in range, plus the OBLA paragraph). Renders are in `staging/_renders/rev_p252.png` to `rev_p265.png`. Every \"Eric's baseline:\" quote was checked against `docs/method-baseline.md` at the cited line. Every `[[wikilink]]` in the 23 files resolves (staging folder or vault). Vault library grepped for each concept (dynamic correspondence, parachute, accentuated region, VO2 max, myoglobin, functional specialisation, factor structure, reactivity coefficient, local muscular endurance, P = F.V, regime of muscular work). Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 checked by web search (PubMed 6036801). Mechanical checks on all 23 files: each has exactly the six `**Section** —` headers and no other em dash, and no `[[wikilink]]` wraps across lines.\n\n**Threshold used for \"When to apply\" sections.** Applying the author's rule to a practical case in the writer's voice is accepted. A row is flagged only where the application adds content the author did not give (a population, a recovery rule, a training reduction, a physics judgment) without an \"Inference:\" label. The fixer should use the same threshold.\n\n## Known source oddities: how the entries handle them\n\n| Oddity | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| Fig 4.21 text (\"hip flexion torque in the air\") vs caption (\"take-off for the triple jump\"), PDF 255 / p.244 | Handled honestly in `heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle` (When NOT, both quoted, figure demoted to illustration). Figure values checked against image: peak about 700-720 N.m near 0.016-0.02 s, below 200 N.m by about 0.06 s, low to 0.160 s. |\n| \"6% ... only 7%\" (Williams et al 1967), PDF 261 / p.250 | Handled honestly in `claim--local-blood-flow-not-vo2max-tracks-competition-period-endurance-gains` (image confirms 6% and 7%; \"do not cite it\"). |\n| Equation 4.1 placement and impulse \"where s is the displacement\", PDF 257 / p.246 | Both oddities recorded correctly in `claim--power-equals-force-times-velocity-only-when-force-is-constant`. But that entry has a separate physics error (see its FIX row). |\n| 4.3.3 effort rule (\"not less ... even exceed\" vs \"moderate amount of effort\"), PDF 256-257 / pp.245-246 | Handled honestly in `principle--training-effort-must-match-or-exceed-sport-effort-judged-by-movement-speed` (both quoted, reconciliation labelled Inference). |\n| Aerobic/anaerobic antagonism offered p.249, questioned p.250 | Handled honestly in `claim--vo2max-alone-does-not-determine-endurance-performance` (Why it works keeps both) and `claim--local-blood-flow-...` (When NOT). |\n| Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 | Handled honestly in `claim--strength-training-raises-haemoglobin-myoglobin-and-aids-distance-sport`. Reviewer confirmed independently: PubMed 6036801, \"Augmentation of skeletal muscle myoglobin by a program of treadmill running,\" Am J Physiol 1967;213(3):783-5. The entry's citation details are correct. |\n| Table column sums | Table 4.1 sums checked: 29.6+19.6+13.0+10.5+6.5 = 79.2; 27.4+23.4+18.5+11.8 = 81.1 (entry says about 79% and 81%: correct). Table 4.2: 35.9+23.3+16.8+2.7+8.9 = 87.6; 36.5+21.9+19.8+10.9 = 89.1 (entry says about 88% and 89%: correct). Not flagged by the writer: Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9), against factor ordering (see skater FIX row). |\n\n## Entry verdicts\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem (entry quote / source quote with page) | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence.md | FIX | When NOT, Inference: \"when the criteria conflict (for example, matching amplitude may require an awkward position that breaks the regime of work, as the authors' own Fig 4.22 discussion shows, PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245), the text gives no ranking among them.\" The source says the opposite: \"Following these requirements can sometimes lead to such initial positions ... which are incongruous and artificial (Fig 4.22). However, this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria\" (PDF 256 / p.245). The authors deny a conflict; nothing there mentions the regime of work. Rest checked: five criteria list at PDF 252 / p.241; \"All sporting movement is specific and goal-directed\", \"One should not refer to strength in general\", \"an adequate conditioning regime\" at PDF 252; \"success in selecting the means ... biomechanics of the movements\" at PDF 259 / p.248; \"only part of the process\" at PDF 266 / p.255 (opened); baseline line 103 quote exact. | Replace that sentence with: \"The text gives no ranking among the criteria. The authors say awkward positi\n\n... [18472 characters truncated] ...\n\n' jump in \"energetic efficiency of executing specific work\" (2.7% to 36.5%)\" relies on that value. Rest checked: all nine values and labels against image; sums 87.6 and 89.1; \"sharp rise\", \"combined as one factor (i.e. aerobic efficiency)\", \"anaerobic power increases slightly (factor III)\" across PDF 263-264; conclusion quote; glycolysis conflict cross-referenced correctly; baseline line 172. | (1) In When NOT add: \"Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9), against the order of factors by share (verified against the page image); 2.7 may be a misprint (12.7 would restore the order and bring the column to about 98%), but the source gives no correction, so treat the 2.7 value as unclear.\" (2) In When to apply replace the Inference with: \"Inference: the rise of \"energetic efficiency of executing specific work\" to the first factor at Master of Sport level (36.5%) is consistent with that teaching point; the Class 1 value for the same factor (2.7) is unclear, so the size of the change should not be quoted.\" |\n\n## `_book.md` (4.3 and 4.4 rows, newest batch note)\n\n| Item | Verdict | Problem | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Rows 4.3 (241-247 / 252-258, done, 13) and 4.4 (248-254 / 259-265, done, 10) | GO | Entry counts match the scope list (13 files with chapter 4.3.x, 10 with 4.4). Page ranges match the source; the batch note explains that 4.3.6 runs onto PDF 259 and that PDF 265 / p.254 is blank (confirmed: text layer is only \"254\"). | None. |\n| Chapter 4 parent row (line 96: \"in progress \\| 6 (see section rows below)\") | FIX | The batch note says \"Chapter 4 is now complete; resume at Chapter 5\" and admits the parent row \"was not changed in this session.\" The map contradicts itself. | Set line 96 status to \"done\" and the count to the Chapter 4 total, and delete the sentence \"The Chapter 4 parent row still reads \"in progress \\| 6\" and was not changed in this session.\" from the batch note. |\n| Batch note content | GO | Section names, page spans, figure/table pages checked (PDF 253-257, 260-264), contested list and Pattengale note all match the entries. | None. |\n\n## Duplicates\n\nNone. The vault has Evans's applied wrestling case study (`elite-sports-performance--evans/case-study--dynamic-correspondence-applied-to-wrestling-takedown`) and Supertraining Ch1's ten-dimension specificity entry, which says Ch4.3 was \"not yet ingested\". `framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence` is the first primary-source entry for the criteria and links both. No vault entry covers parachutes, the accentuated region, the VO2 max arguments, myoglobin, functional specialisation levels or the two factor tables. The RFD heuristic adds the impulse-comparison and correspondence angle beyond `principle--rate-of-force-development-as-independent-limiter`.\n\n## Missing ideas (covered pages, not captured)\n\nThe batch captures the covered pages well. Only candidates:\n1. OBLA as the practical target (PDF 260 / p.249): \"Practical improvement of the metabolic processes in endurance sports is associated with ... raising the Onset of Blood Lactate Accumulation (OBLA),\" with \"Since OBLA depends on VO2 max ...\" This sits only inside the contested entry's When NOT. Optional: a short claim entry on OBLA as the endurance target, or a sentence in the What it is of `claim--endurance-rests-on-muscle-oxidative-and-strength-qualities-not-vo2max`.\n2. Nothing else of importance. (PDF 252's 4.2.9 muscle isolation passage belongs to the earlier batch and already has an entry.)\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Counts: GO 15, FIX 8, NO-GO 0 (entries), plus 1 `_book.md` FIX.\n\nRequired fixes:\n1. `claim--power-equals-force-times-velocity-only-when-force-is-constant`: correct the physics (instantaneous P = F·v holds for any force), retitle, rescope `proven`, rewrite the When NOT line.\n2. `framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence`: replace the Fig 4.22 \"criteria conflict\" inference; the authors say awkward positions arise only when the criteria are ignored.\n3. `heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle`: add the dropped \"However, this occurs only when ...\" sentence to the Fig 4.22 passage.\n4. `case-study--skater-factor-structure-by-qualification`: flag Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV = 2.7 as out of order and unclear; stop quoting the 2.7 to 36.5 jump.\n5. `case-study--high-jumper-factor-structure-by-qualification`: label \"less to plantarflexor power\" as Inference.\n6. `claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence`: label the \"heavy athletes, athletes returning from lower-limb injury\" populations as Inference.\n7. `heuristic--same-exercise-different-regime-boxer-vs-shot-putter`: label or drop \"full recovery\".\n8. `heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release`: replace \"standard fluid mechanics\" with the author's own words plus a labelled Inference.\n9. `_book.md`: set the Chapter 4 parent row to done and remove the sentence that says it was left unchanged.\n(eval):1: ===== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HHkaC947EH464tms5KMQy"}]},"uuid":"f1c85727-7f28-4b6e-b28a-5a7585c5f878","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:45:01.376Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# Review: Supertraining Ch4.3-4.4 (23 entries), falsification pass\n\nReviewer: Claude Opus (independent of the writer). Date: 2026-10-03.\nSource: *Supertraining* 6th Expanded, PDF idx 252-265 (printed 241-254). Page key: PDF idx = printed + 11.\nMethod: text layer extracted with pymupdf for every covered page; page images rendered at 150 dpi and opened for PDF 253, 254, 255, 256, 257, 260, 261, 262, 263, 264 (every figure, table and equation in range, plus the OBLA paragraph). Renders are in `staging/_renders/rev_p252.png` to `rev_p265.png`. Every \"Eric's baseline:\" quote was checked against `docs/method-baseline.md` at the cited line. Every `[[wikilink]]` in the 23 files resolves (staging folder or vault). Vault library grepped for each concept (dynamic correspondence, parachute, accentuated region, VO2 max, myoglobin, functional specialisation, factor structure, reactivity coefficient, local muscular endurance, P = F.V, regime of muscular work). Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 checked by web search (PubMed 6036801). Mechanical checks on all 23 files: each has exactly the six `**Section** —` headers and no other em dash, and no `[[wikilink]]` wraps across lines.\n\n**Threshold used for \"When to apply\" sections.** Applying the author's rule to a practical case in the writer's voice is accepted. A row is flagged only where the application adds content the author did not give (a population, a recovery rule, a training reduction, a physics judgment) without an \"Inference:\" label. The fixer should use the same threshold.\n\n## Known source oddities: how the entries handle them\n\n| Oddity | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| Fig 4.21 text (\"hip flexion torque in the air\") vs caption (\"take-off for the triple jump\"), PDF 255 / p.244 | Handled honestly in `heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle` (When NOT, both quoted, figure demoted to illustration). Figure values checked against image: peak about 700-720 N.m near 0.016-0.02 s, below 200 N.m by about 0.06 s, low to 0.160 s. |\n| \"6% ... only 7%\" (Williams et al 1967), PDF 261 / p.250 | Handled honestly in `claim--local-blood-flow-not-vo2max-tracks-competition-period-endurance-gains` (image confirms 6% and 7%; \"do not cite it\"). |\n| Equation 4.1 placement and impulse \"where s is the displacement\", PDF 257 / p.246 | Both oddities recorded correctly in `claim--power-equals-force-times-velocity-only-when-force-is-constant`. But that entry has a separate physics error (see its FIX row). |\n| 4.3.3 effort rule (\"not less ... even exceed\" vs \"moderate amount of effort\"), PDF 256-257 / pp.245-246 | Handled honestly in `principle--training-effort-must-match-or-exceed-sport-effort-judged-by-movement-speed` (both quoted, reconciliation labelled Inference). |\n| Aerobic/anaerobic antagonism offered p.249, questioned p.250 | Handled honestly in `claim--vo2max-alone-does-not-determine-endurance-performance` (Why it works keeps both) and `claim--local-blood-flow-...` (When NOT). |\n| Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 | Handled honestly in `claim--strength-training-raises-haemoglobin-myoglobin-and-aids-distance-sport`. Reviewer confirmed independently: PubMed 6036801, \"Augmentation of skeletal muscle myoglobin by a program of treadmill running,\" Am J Physiol 1967;213(3):783-5. The entry's citation details are correct. |\n| Table column sums | Table 4.1 sums checked: 29.6+19.6+13.0+10.5+6.5 = 79.2; 27.4+23.4+18.5+11.8 = 81.1 (entry says about 79% and 81%: correct). Table 4.2: 35.9+23.3+16.8+2.7+8.9 = 87.6; 36.5+21.9+19.8+10.9 = 89.1 (entry says about 88% and 89%: correct). Not flagged by the writer: Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9), against factor ordering (see skater FIX row). |\n\n## Entry verdicts\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem (entry quote / source quote with page) | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence.md | FIX | When NOT, Inference: \"when the criteria conflict (for example, matching amplitude may require an awkward position that breaks the regime of work, as the authors' own Fig 4.22 discussion shows, PDF p. 256 / printed p. 245), the text gives no ranking among them.\" The source says the opposite: \"Following these requirements can sometimes lead to such initial positions ... which are incongruous and artificial (Fig 4.22). However, this occurs only when an exercise is attempted which fails to take into consideration the appropriate criteria\" (PDF 256 / p.245). The authors deny a conflict; nothing there mentions the regime of work. Rest checked: five criteria list at PDF 252 / p.241; \"All sporting movement is specific and goal-directed\", \"One should not refer to strength in general\", \"an adequate conditioning regime\" at PDF 252; \"success in selecting the means ... biomechanics of the movements\" at PDF 259 / p.248; \"only part of the process\" at PDF 266 / p.255 (opened); baseline line 103 quote exact. | Replace that sentence with: \"The text gives no ranking among the criteria. The authors say awkward positi\n\n... [18472 characters truncated] ...\n\n' jump in \"energetic efficiency of executing specific work\" (2.7% to 36.5%)\" relies on that value. Rest checked: all nine values and labels against image; sums 87.6 and 89.1; \"sharp rise\", \"combined as one factor (i.e. aerobic efficiency)\", \"anaerobic power increases slightly (factor III)\" across PDF 263-264; conclusion quote; glycolysis conflict cross-referenced correctly; baseline line 172. | (1) In When NOT add: \"Class 1 factor IV (2.7) is smaller than factor V (8.9), against the order of factors by share (verified against the page image); 2.7 may be a misprint (12.7 would restore the order and bring the column to about 98%), but the source gives no correction, so treat the 2.7 value as unclear.\" (2) In When to apply replace the Inference with: \"Inference: the rise of \"energetic efficiency of executing specific work\" to the first factor at Master of Sport level (36.5%) is consistent with that teaching point; the Class 1 value for the same factor (2.7) is unclear, so the size of the change should not be quoted.\" |\n\n## `_book.md` (4.3 and 4.4 rows, newest batch note)\n\n| Item | Verdict | Problem | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Rows 4.3 (241-247 / 252-258, done, 13) and 4.4 (248-254 / 259-265, done, 10) | GO | Entry counts match the scope list (13 files with chapter 4.3.x, 10 with 4.4). Page ranges match the source; the batch note explains that 4.3.6 runs onto PDF 259 and that PDF 265 / p.254 is blank (confirmed: text layer is only \"254\"). | None. |\n| Chapter 4 parent row (line 96: \"in progress \\| 6 (see section rows below)\") | FIX | The batch note says \"Chapter 4 is now complete; resume at Chapter 5\" and admits the parent row \"was not changed in this session.\" The map contradicts itself. | Set line 96 status to \"done\" and the count to the Chapter 4 total, and delete the sentence \"The Chapter 4 parent row still reads \"in progress \\| 6\" and was not changed in this session.\" from the batch note. |\n| Batch note content | GO | Section names, page spans, figure/table pages checked (PDF 253-257, 260-264), contested list and Pattengale note all match the entries. | None. |\n\n## Duplicates\n\nNone. The vault has Evans's applied wrestling case study (`elite-sports-performance--evans/case-study--dynamic-correspondence-applied-to-wrestling-takedown`) and Supertraining Ch1's ten-dimension specificity entry, which says Ch4.3 was \"not yet ingested\". `framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence` is the first primary-source entry for the criteria and links both. No vault entry covers parachutes, the accentuated region, the VO2 max arguments, myoglobin, functional specialisation levels or the two factor tables. The RFD heuristic adds the impulse-comparison and correspondence angle beyond `principle--rate-of-force-development-as-independent-limiter`.\n\n## Missing ideas (covered pages, not captured)\n\nThe batch captures the covered pages well. Only candidates:\n1. OBLA as the practical target (PDF 260 / p.249): \"Practical improvement of the metabolic processes in endurance sports is associated with ... raising the Onset of Blood Lactate Accumulation (OBLA),\" with \"Since OBLA depends on VO2 max ...\" This sits only inside the contested entry's When NOT. Optional: a short claim entry on OBLA as the endurance target, or a sentence in the What it is of `claim--endurance-rests-on-muscle-oxidative-and-strength-qualities-not-vo2max`.\n2. Nothing else of importance. (PDF 252's 4.2.9 muscle isolation passage belongs to the earlier batch and already has an entry.)\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Counts: GO 15, FIX 8, NO-GO 0 (entries), plus 1 `_book.md` FIX.\n\nRequired fixes:\n1. `claim--power-equals-force-times-velocity-only-when-force-is-constant`: correct the physics (instantaneous P = F·v holds for any force), retitle, rescope `proven`, rewrite the When NOT line.\n2. `framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence`: replace the Fig 4.22 \"criteria conflict\" inference; the authors say awkward positions arise only when the criteria are ignored.\n3. `heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle`: add the dropped \"However, this occurs only when ...\" sentence to the Fig 4.22 passage.\n4. `case-study--skater-factor-structure-by-qualification`: flag Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV = 2.7 as out of order and unclear; stop quoting the 2.7 to 36.5 jump.\n5. `case-study--high-jumper-factor-structure-by-qualification`: label \"less to plantarflexor power\" as Inference.\n6. `claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence`: label the \"heavy athletes, athletes returning from lower-limb injury\" populations as Inference.\n7. `heuristic--same-exercise-different-regime-boxer-vs-shot-putter`: label or drop \"full recovery\".\n8. `heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release`: replace \"standard fluid mechanics\" with the author's own words plus a labelled Inference.\n9. `_book.md`: set the Chapter 4 parent row to done and remove the sentence that says it was left unchanged.\n(eval):1: ===== not found","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"91ccf4a3-563b-4e9e-aa79-3f5875e7dd0e","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
