{"parentUuid":"fc33349a-899e-489a-870b-f2b5971a9907","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a07e06bc199bf998d","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffZy18VncXRZTiE6qRkf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011psaPDEusjWKNX6Q6CtN3E","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs && for n in 41 61 97 102 105 108 116 117 119 142 173 182 183 184; do echo \"L$n: $(sed -n ${n}p method-baseline.md | cut -c1-400)\"; done; cat /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py | head -60","description":"Show baseline lines and lint script"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7867,"cache_read_input_tokens":247365,"output_tokens":443,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":232},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7867},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":247365,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7867,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011psaPDEusjWKNX6Q6CtN3E":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs && for n in 41 61 97 102 105 108 116 117 119 142 173 182 183 184; do echo \"L$n: $(sed -n ${n}p method-baseline.md | cut -c1-400)\"; done; cat /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py | head -60","description":"Show baseline lines and lint script"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffZxn4RtosZ7A3Q4H8Ki","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc86eda1-c25b-4218-957b-f85395659d98","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:50:22.863Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"dc86eda1-c25b-4218-957b-f85395659d98","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"624a8cec-33fa-4c0a-a445-c72ce718e6ab","agentId":"a07e06bc199bf998d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011psaPDEusjWKNX6Q6CtN3E","type":"tool_result","content":"L41: - \"Knowledge from experience\" as a stated operating value: safety first, keep things simple, teach basic movement skills and basic lifts before anything advanced, treat strength as the base, and require bodyweight competency before loaded work. **Inferred (transcript + Week 1 slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.4-5; week1-lecture.md p.12]\nL61: - No sport performs true 1RM testing. Maxes are projected from observation plus the athlete's history. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q10): \"things are ballparked based on other information we're grabbing on the athlete: watching them move in real time, then using historical context to make future programming decisions around projected 1RMs.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q10)**\nL97: - Issurin's residual training effects (speed fades fastest, 5 ± 3 days; Block Periodization PDF p. 35, as cited in `docs/synthesis/peaking-and-taper-in-season-football.md`) drive speed programming. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q16): \"I believe Issurin. It drives our speed programming in the off-season and what drives sprinting recommendations in season.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q16)** See\nL102: - Exercise selection is organized on a spectrum from general preparation through specific preparation, specific development, to competitive exercises (Bondarchuk), replacing the loose and often-misapplied idea of \"sport specific.\" **Inferred (transcript + slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.13-16; week1-lecture.md pp.32-36]\nL105: - Off-season strength work prioritizes relative strength and technique first; already-strong athletes shift more time toward strength-speed/speed-strength work. In-season, the stated rule is \"maintain intensity, reduce volume\" rather than trying to build strength while managing a full competition schedule. **Inferred (transcript + shared slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.20-21; hh\nL108: - Strength's residual training effect is treated as roughly 30 days; a minimal retention dose is still trained within that window, even during lower-strength-emphasis blocks. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.24-25] Inference: consistent with Eric siding with Issurin (Q16), whose strength residual is 30 ± 5 days, though Q16 was about speed and he did not claim this\nL116: - For football specifically, the stated priority stack is: Goal 1, alactic and aerobic capacity/power for fall-camp demands; Goal 2, the same two systems for game demands; glycolytic conditioning is treated as a \"worst case scenario\" to be absorbed incidentally through camp and practice rather than programmed as a primary target. **Explicit** [class-4-2026.md pp.34, 39]; claimed again in the inter\nL117: - Glycolytic conditioning is still not a primary target in season, but staff do program it in the off-season. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q19): \"It does hold up, but our staff does program it in the off-season.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q19)**\nL119: - The anaerobic-threshold heart rate in use is the age-based method (the slide deck's max HR = 220-age for men, 226-age for women, threshold at about 85% of that [class-4-2026.md p.27]). Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q20): \"Age-based.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q20)** Resolves Tension 6.\nL142: - Progressions in exercise selection, volume, and intensity are kept smooth and gradual by design; abrupt, large changes are treated as a direct injury-risk driver, not just a training-quality issue. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.27]\nL173: - Basic movement skills and basic lifts are taught before anything advanced, on the observed premise that many incoming athletes have high sport-specific skill from early specialization but poor general movement competency. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.4-5]\nL182: - Training-compatibility is an explicit constraint on programming: incompatible qualities (e.g., maximal strength work and glycolytic-capacity work) are not both targeted at full intensity in the same block — \"you can't ride two horses with one saddle.\" Compatible qualities are trained together; the rest are trained at a retention dose. **Inferred (transcript + slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-tr\nL183: - An annual plan is treated as a flexible roadmap, not a fixed contract: lay out the competition calendar, key non-training dates (holidays, exam weeks), and phase-by-phase volume/intensity waves, then adapt the route as circumstances change while still reaching the same destination. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.22-23; 2026-02-05-hp5355-class3-transcript.md pp\nL184: - Training residual effects set the retraining cadence: aerobic capacity and max strength both need re-exposure roughly every 30 days; speed needs re-exposure roughly every 5 days or tissue readiness for max-velocity work degrades. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.27] Inference: these are Issurin's figures, and Eric sides with Issurin (interview 2026-09-28, Q16), s\n\"\"\"Mechanical pre-promotion lint for Flint staged library folders.\n\nUsage: python scripts/lint_library.py <book-folder> [<book-folder> ...]\nChecks: body em dashes (header separators allowed), unresolved [[links]] (against staging\nlibrary + vault), review-history narration, confidence values, required sections.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSTAGING = Path(\"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library\")\nVAULT = Path(\"/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library\")\nHEADER = re.compile(r\"^\\*\\*[^*]+\\*\\* —\")\nHISTORY = re.compile(r\"prior version|earlier draft|NO-GO|round[- ]1|round[- ]2|fix pass|fixer|this revision|previous version\", re.I)\nCONF = {\"proven\", \"supported\", \"untested\", \"contested\"}\nSECTIONS = [\"**What it is**\", \"**When NOT to apply**\"]\n\nknown = set()\nfor root in (STAGING, VAULT):\n    for p in root.rglob(\"*.md\"):\n        known.add(p.stem)\n        known.add(p.relative_to(root).with_suffix(\"\").as_posix())\n        known.add(p.parent.name + \"/\" + p.stem)\n\nproblems = 0\nfor folder in sys.argv[1:]:\n    for f in sorted(Path(folder).glob(\"*.md\")):\n        text = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        issues = []\n        body_dash = [i + 1 for i, line in enumerate(text.splitlines())\n                     if \"—\" in HEADER.sub(\"\", line)]\n        if body_dash:\n            issues.append(f\"body em dash lines {body_dash[:8]}\")\n        for link in re.findall(r\"\\[\\[([^\\]|#]+)\", text):\n            link = link.strip().removesuffix(\".md\")\n            if link not in known and link.split(\"/\")[-1] not in known:\n                issues.append(f\"unresolved [[{link}]]\")\n        if not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n            m = re.search(r\"^confidence:\\s*(\\S+)\", text, re.M)\n            if not m or m.group(1).strip(\"\\\"'\") not in CONF:\n                issues.append(f\"confidence={m.group(1) if m else 'missing'}\")\n            for s in SECTIONS:\n                if s not in text:\n                    issues.append(f\"missing {s}\")\n            h = HISTORY.findall(text)\n            if h:\n                issues.append(f\"review-history words {sorted(set(x.lower() for x in h))}\")\n        if issues:\n            problems += len(issues)\n            print(f\"{f.parent.name}/{f.name}: \" + \"; \".join(issues))\nprint(f\"TOTAL ISSUES: {problems}\")","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e41abfd2-6e4c-4ed3-8749-02cfd2e6b929","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:50:23.103Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"L41: - \"Knowledge from experience\" as a stated operating value: safety first, keep things simple, teach basic movement skills and basic lifts before anything advanced, treat strength as the base, and require bodyweight competency before loaded work. **Inferred (transcript + Week 1 slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.4-5; week1-lecture.md p.12]\nL61: - No sport performs true 1RM testing. Maxes are projected from observation plus the athlete's history. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q10): \"things are ballparked based on other information we're grabbing on the athlete: watching them move in real time, then using historical context to make future programming decisions around projected 1RMs.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q10)**\nL97: - Issurin's residual training effects (speed fades fastest, 5 ± 3 days; Block Periodization PDF p. 35, as cited in `docs/synthesis/peaking-and-taper-in-season-football.md`) drive speed programming. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q16): \"I believe Issurin. It drives our speed programming in the off-season and what drives sprinting recommendations in season.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q16)** See\nL102: - Exercise selection is organized on a spectrum from general preparation through specific preparation, specific development, to competitive exercises (Bondarchuk), replacing the loose and often-misapplied idea of \"sport specific.\" **Inferred (transcript + slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.13-16; week1-lecture.md pp.32-36]\nL105: - Off-season strength work prioritizes relative strength and technique first; already-strong athletes shift more time toward strength-speed/speed-strength work. In-season, the stated rule is \"maintain intensity, reduce volume\" rather than trying to build strength while managing a full competition schedule. **Inferred (transcript + shared slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.20-21; hh\nL108: - Strength's residual training effect is treated as roughly 30 days; a minimal retention dose is still trained within that window, even during lower-strength-emphasis blocks. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.24-25] Inference: consistent with Eric siding with Issurin (Q16), whose strength residual is 30 ± 5 days, though Q16 was about speed and he did not claim this\nL116: - For football specifically, the stated priority stack is: Goal 1, alactic and aerobic capacity/power for fall-camp demands; Goal 2, the same two systems for game demands; glycolytic conditioning is treated as a \"worst case scenario\" to be absorbed incidentally through camp and practice rather than programmed as a primary target. **Explicit** [class-4-2026.md pp.34, 39]; claimed again in the inter\nL117: - Glycolytic conditioning is still not a primary target in season, but staff do program it in the off-season. Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q19): \"It does hold up, but our staff does program it in the off-season.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q19)**\nL119: - The anaerobic-threshold heart rate in use is the age-based method (the slide deck's max HR = 220-age for men, 226-age for women, threshold at about 85% of that [class-4-2026.md p.27]). Eric (interview 2026-09-28, Q20): \"Age-based.\" **Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q20)** Resolves Tension 6.\nL142: - Progressions in exercise selection, volume, and intensity are kept smooth and gradual by design; abrupt, large changes are treated as a direct injury-risk driver, not just a training-quality issue. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.27]\nL173: - Basic movement skills and basic lifts are taught before anything advanced, on the observed premise that many incoming athletes have high sport-specific skill from early specialization but poor general movement competency. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.4-5]\nL182: - Training-compatibility is an explicit constraint on programming: incompatible qualities (e.g., maximal strength work and glycolytic-capacity work) are not both targeted at full intensity in the same block — \"you can't ride two horses with one saddle.\" Compatible qualities are trained together; the rest are trained at a retention dose. **Inferred (transcript + slides)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-tr\nL183: - An annual plan is treated as a flexible roadmap, not a fixed contract: lay out the competition calendar, key non-training dates (holidays, exam weeks), and phase-by-phase volume/intensity waves, then adapt the route as circumstances change while still reaching the same destination. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md pp.22-23; 2026-02-05-hp5355-class3-transcript.md pp\nL184: - Training residual effects set the retraining cadence: aerobic capacity and max strength both need re-exposure roughly every 30 days; speed needs re-exposure roughly every 5 days or tissue readiness for max-velocity work degrades. **Inferred (transcript)** [01192022-hp5355-class1-transcript.md p.27] Inference: these are Issurin's figures, and Eric sides with Issurin (interview 2026-09-28, Q16), s\n\"\"\"Mechanical pre-promotion lint for Flint staged library folders.\n\nUsage: python scripts/lint_library.py <book-folder> [<book-folder> ...]\nChecks: body em dashes (header separators allowed), unresolved [[links]] (against staging\nlibrary + vault), review-history narration, confidence values, required sections.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSTAGING = Path(\"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library\")\nVAULT = Path(\"/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library\")\nHEADER = re.compile(r\"^\\*\\*[^*]+\\*\\* —\")\nHISTORY = re.compile(r\"prior version|earlier draft|NO-GO|round[- ]1|round[- ]2|fix pass|fixer|this revision|previous version\", re.I)\nCONF = {\"proven\", \"supported\", \"untested\", \"contested\"}\nSECTIONS = [\"**What it is**\", \"**When NOT to apply**\"]\n\nknown = set()\nfor root in (STAGING, VAULT):\n    for p in root.rglob(\"*.md\"):\n        known.add(p.stem)\n        known.add(p.relative_to(root).with_suffix(\"\").as_posix())\n        known.add(p.parent.name + \"/\" + p.stem)\n\nproblems = 0\nfor folder in sys.argv[1:]:\n    for f in sorted(Path(folder).glob(\"*.md\")):\n        text = f.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        issues = []\n        body_dash = [i + 1 for i, line in enumerate(text.splitlines())\n                     if \"—\" in HEADER.sub(\"\", line)]\n        if body_dash:\n            issues.append(f\"body em dash lines {body_dash[:8]}\")\n        for link in re.findall(r\"\\[\\[([^\\]|#]+)\", text):\n            link = link.strip().removesuffix(\".md\")\n            if link not in known and link.split(\"/\")[-1] not in known:\n                issues.append(f\"unresolved [[{link}]]\")\n        if not f.name.startswith(\"_\"):\n            m = re.search(r\"^confidence:\\s*(\\S+)\", text, re.M)\n            if not m or m.group(1).strip(\"\\\"'\") not in CONF:\n                issues.append(f\"confidence={m.group(1) if m else 'missing'}\")\n            for s in SECTIONS:\n                if s not in text:\n                    issues.append(f\"missing {s}\")\n            h = HISTORY.findall(text)\n            if h:\n                issues.append(f\"review-history words {sorted(set(x.lower() for x in h))}\")\n        if issues:\n            problems += len(issues)\n            print(f\"{f.parent.name}/{f.name}: \" + \"; \".join(issues))\nprint(f\"TOTAL ISSUES: {problems}\")","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc86eda1-c25b-4218-957b-f85395659d98","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
