{"parentUuid":"ad0487f2-ea18-4018-bc99-6b5733aadc4b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"13b2e94d-1b2a-4672-944b-f2e4cd21284b","agentId":"a07e06bc199bf998d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L1b526MpTHNSb9JSYJETNB","type":"tool_result","content":"PERTRAINING ADDENDUM tremely concentrated loads lead to a more significant decrease in functional indices and to a  disruption in adaptation (graph fj). When using concentrated loads orientated to achieving the LDTE, the methods used should  not be extremely intense. Concentration, in one of the single purpose loads, is already in­ tensification of the training effect and to increase it with highly intense means of training  does not follow. Realization of LDTE of concentrated loads is served by moderate increases in work volume  and gradually increasing intensity (B). .  The duration of the appearance of LDTE is determined by the volume and duration of the  concentrated loads used. In principle, the steady appearance of LDTE (t2 ) is equal to the du­ ration of the stage (ti). In real conditions of training high level athletes, the tendency has  been for the stages to last anywhere from 4-12 weeks. It follows, however, to keep in mind  that the appearance of LDTE has an independent character and to a significant degree, de­ pends upon the ability of the athlete to withstand volume loads and the ability of his body  for recovery. The same volume loads in two athletes having the same","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b6d64e7d-0c37-4bca-a7ee-9f84bcd44651","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:07:10.224Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"PERTRAINING ADDENDUM tremely concentrated loads lead to a more significant decrease in functional indices and to a  disruption in adaptation (graph fj). When using concentrated loads orientated to achieving the LDTE, the methods used should  not be extremely intense. Concentration, in one of the single purpose loads, is already in­ tensification of the training effect and to increase it with highly intense means of training  does not follow. Realization of LDTE of concentrated loads is served by moderate increases in work volume  and gradually increasing intensity (B). .  The duration of the appearance of LDTE is determined by the volume and duration of the  concentrated loads used. In principle, the steady appearance of LDTE (t2 ) is equal to the du­ ration of the stage (ti). In real conditions of training high level athletes, the tendency has  been for the stages to last anywhere from 4-12 weeks. It follows, however, to keep in mind  that the appearance of LDTE has an independent character and to a significant degree, de­ pends upon the ability of the athlete to withstand volume loads and the ability of his body  for recovery. The same volume loads in two athletes having the same","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad0487f2-ea18-4018-bc99-6b5733aadc4b","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
